'''Jak Sivrak''' was a [[Troig]] [[Gender|male]] who lived during the [[New Republic Era|era]] of the [[New Republic]]. Sivrak served as the announcer of the [[Racer|races]] that were held on the ''[[Colossus]]'' refueling platform on the [[ocean]] [[planet]] of [[Castilon]].<ref name="The Recruit" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Jak Sivrak is a character created and developed for the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' animated series, and is voiced by [[Greg Proops]], who previously voiced [[Fodesinbeed Annodue|Fode]] in [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''The Phantom Menace'']] and [[Tal Merrik]] in [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''The Clone Wars'']]. Sivrak's name is a play on the name [[Lak Sivrak]].<ref name="Syfy">{{WebCite|url=https://www.syfy.com/syfywire/star-wars-resistance-harbors-crazy-deep-cuts-and-will-cross-over-with-the-force-awakens|text=Star Wars Resistance harbors crazy deep cuts and will cross over with The Force Awakens|author=Young, Brian|date=2018-10-02|archivedate=20191227161942}}</ref> Sivrak was first pictured in [[Star Wars Adventures (2017)|''Star Wars Adventures'' (2017) 16's]] first accompanying story, "[[All Aces Battle Royale (comic story)|All Aces Battle Royale]]," which published on [[December 19]], [[2018]].<ref name="AABR" /> While not identified in the comic itself, [[Chris "Doc" Wyatt|Chris Wyatt]] confirmed the depiction was intended to be Sivrak in the script.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|otherland71|status/1441559335386042368|Chris "Doc" Wyatt|quote=That was our intention at script, yes.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/eHLYw}}</ref>

